    "site_desc": "This site is established as an urban flux tower within a low-rise residential neighborhood of Phoenix, Arizona known as Maryvale in the West Valley. The site access is managed by the Central Arizona Phoenix Long-term Ecological Research (CAP-LTER) program. This site has been renovated with brand new sensors at the end of 2023.  According to the USDA Soil Survey Map, the soil type is Glender clay loam, with clay loam soil within 18 inches in depth. The neighborhood has low rise homes in small lots along with roads, parks and commercial areas. Outdoor vegetation and pools are highly variable among the homes.",
